Feather is an SMTP mail server that can act as a submission agent (MSA) or
a transfer agent (MTA). Its behaviour is assembled from adapters rather
than configured through a monolithic rule language: authentication, access
control, routing, delivery, spam filtering and message transformation are
each a pluggable stage in a session pipeline defined in the config file.

Bundled adapters cover PAM and password-file authentication, IP and relay
access control, per-domain routing, LMTP, MX and SMTP forwarding delivery,
SPF, DKIM, DMARC, DNSBL, rspamd and SpamAssassin filtering, and quarantine
and header-rewriting transformers.

Feather runs on the BEAM; this port installs a self-contained release that
does not require a separate Erlang or Elixir installation at runtime.
